data: {"type": "insight", "data": {"executive_summary": "On-time delivery ranges from 96.2% for UPS to 70.2% for J.B. Hunt across the five carriers in this dataset. UPS and Old Dominion lead on-time delivery, while J.B. Hunt and XPO trail the overall rate of 88.9%. Because each carrier serves different lanes, modes and shippers, differences in on-time rates reflect those mix factors as well as carrier performance.", "technical_findings": ["Loaded 3,000 rows \u00d7 19 columns from a CSV file. (n = 3,000; high confidence: Read as-is: no layout guessing was needed.)", "on_time_delivery (from Shipment ID) by Carrier (5 groups) (n = 3,000; high confidence: 3000 rows)", "sum Total Charge by Carrier (5 groups) (n = 3,000; high confidence: 3000 rows)", "mean Total Charge by Carrier (5 groups) (n = 3,000; high confidence: 3000 rows)", "Weight: median 669.00, mean 1,129.37, range 1.54 to 8,754.20 (n = 2,995; high confidence: 2995 rows)", "Linehaul: median 147.62, mean 185.04, range 5.64 to 1,069.81 (n = 2,840; high confidence: 2840 rows)", "Fuel Surcharge: median 32.98, mean 41.72, range 1.30 to 258.09 (n = 2,840; high confidence: 2840 rows)", "Accessorials: median 0, mean 20.95, range 0 to 75.00 (n = 2,840; high confidence: 2840 rows)", "Total Charge: median 205.70, mean 247.72, range 6.94 to 1,338.03 (n = 2,840; high confidence: 2840 rows)"], "recommended_actions": [{"priority": 1, "action": "Review J.B. Hunt shipments to identify lanes or modes where late deliveries concentrate, and set a remediation target with the carrier.", "reasoning": "J.B. Hunt's 70.2% on-time rate is the lowest of the five carriers and the furthest below the 88.9% overall rate.", "metric_impact": "J.B. Hunt's 70.2% on-time rate is the lowest of the five carriers and the furthest below the 88.9% overall rate."}, {"priority": 2, "action": "Investigate XPO's 81.9% on-time rate to determine whether specific routes or shipment types are driving late deliveries.", "reasoning": "XPO is the second-lowest performer and addressing it could lift the overall on-time rate.", "metric_impact": "XPO is the second-lowest performer and addressing it could lift the overall on-time rate."}, {"priority": 3, "action": "When reviewing carrier contracts, present on-time rates alongside average Total Charge per shipment to assess the full cost-service trade-off for each carrier.", "reasoning": "Pairing service and cost data gives procurement a more complete basis for carrier negotiations.", "metric_impact": "Pairing service and cost data gives procurement a more complete basis for carrier negotiations."}], "anomaly_alerts": [{"title": "Weight: 7 extreme values", "severity": "medium", "description": "7 Weight values (0.2% of rows) are far outside the usual range. They were kept.", "affected_metric": "Weight", "suggested_investigation": "Verify the largest Weight values against the source records."}, {"title": "Linehaul charge: 11 extreme values", "severity": "medium", "description": "11 Linehaul Charge values (0.4% of rows) are far outside the usual range. They were kept.", "affected_metric": "Linehaul", "suggested_investigation": "Verify the largest Linehaul Charge values against the source records."}, {"title": "Fuel surcharge: 14 extreme values", "severity": "medium", "description": "14 Fuel Surcharge values (0.5% of rows) are far outside the usual range. They were kept.", "affected_metric": "Fuel Surcharge", "suggested_investigation": "Verify the largest Fuel Surcharge values against the source records."}, {"title": "Total charge: 11 extreme values", "severity": "medium", "description": "11 Total Charge values (0.4% of rows) are far outside the usual range. They were kept.", "affected_metric": "Total Charge", "suggested_investigation": "Verify the largest Total Charge values against the source records."}, {"title": "How these numbers are counted", "severity": "low", "description": "Read as logistics data (on-time delivery, average transit time, cost per shipment, cost per lb, shipments). Rates pool their parts (on-time, OTIF, fill and cost per lb are totals divided, never averages of per-shipment rates). On time means on or before the promised date, dates as written (local); an early delivery is on time. Transit is in calendar days from the ship date. Cost is in the main currency only. 62 cancelled rows are left out of every count and rate. The data covers 10 months, so month-over-month changes may be seasonal (a peak season); there is no same month last year to compare with. 102 rows in currencies other than USD are left out of every figure, counts and on-time rates too, so the figures side by side read the same shipments. A carrier's figures depend on its lanes, modes and shippers: a difference between carriers is an association, not the carrier's doing, and every rate is given with its number of shipments.", "affected_metric": "", "suggested_investigation": ""}], "proactive_questions": ["Do J.B. Hunt's late deliveries concentrate on specific lanes, shipping modes or origin-destination pairs that could be shifted to better-performing carriers?", "How do on-time rates for each carrier change month over month across the 10-month period \u2014 are late deliveries worsening, improving or stable?", "When shipment mix (mode, lane length, weight) is held constant, do the on-time rate differences between carriers narrow or persist?"], "methodology_notes": "Cleaning (cleaning rules-v1): Parsed numbers or dates in 2 column(s). Merged label spelling variants in 1 column(s). Grouped missing labels as 'Unknown' in 1 column(s). Left missing values as missing in 2 column(s); nothing was imputed. Outliers flagged (kept) in: Fuel Surcharge, Linehaul, Total Charge, Weight. Final dataset: 3000 rows (started with 3000). Analysis (analysis v9) computed: eda, segment, source. Descriptive statistics use the non-missing values of each column.", "executive_view": {"headline": "On-time delivery ranges from 96.2% for UPS to 70.2% for J.B. Hunt across the five carriers in this dataset.", "headline_evidence_ids": ["seg:Carrier/Shipment ID:ratio:on_time_delivery"], "paragraphs": [{"text": "UPS and Old Dominion lead on-time delivery, while J.B. Hunt and XPO trail the overall rate of 88.9%.", "evidence_ids": ["seg:Carrier/Shipment ID:ratio:on_time_delivery"], "typed": null}, {"text": "Because each carrier serves different lanes, modes and shippers, differences in on-time rates reflect those mix factors as well as carrier performance.", "evidence_ids": ["seg:Carrier/Shipment ID:ratio:on_time_delivery"], "typed": null}], "findings": [{"text": "On time delivery by Carrier: UPS highest (96.2%), J.B. Hunt lowest (70.2%).", "evidence_ids": ["seg:Carrier/Shipment ID:ratio:on_time_delivery"], "typed": null}, {"text": "FedEx Freight sits near the middle at 90.7%, close to the overall rate.", "evidence_ids": ["seg:Carrier/Shipment ID:ratio:on_time_delivery"], "typed": null}, {"text": "XPO delivers on time 81.9% of the time and J.B. Hunt 70.2%, both below the overall rate of 88.9%.", "evidence_ids": ["seg:Carrier/Shipment ID:ratio:on_time_delivery"], "typed": null}, {"text": "UPS also averages the lowest Total Charge at $166.21 per shipment, while Old Dominion averages $312.05.", "evidence_ids": ["seg:Carrier/Total Charge"], "typed": null}], "action_items": [{"action": "Review J.B. Hunt shipments to identify lanes or modes where late deliveries concentrate, and set a remediation target with the carrier.", "expected_impact": "J.B. Hunt's 70.2% on-time rate is the lowest of the five carriers and the furthest below the 88.9% overall rate.", "evidence_ids": ["seg:Carrier/Shipment ID:ratio:on_time_delivery"]}, {"action": "Investigate XPO's 81.9% on-time rate to determine whether specific routes or shipment types are driving late deliveries.", "expected_impact": "XPO is the second-lowest performer and addressing it could lift the overall on-time rate.", "evidence_ids": ["seg:Carrier/Shipment ID:ratio:on_time_delivery"]}, {"action": "When reviewing carrier contracts, present on-time rates alongside average Total Charge per shipment to assess the full cost-service trade-off for each carrier.", "expected_impact": "Pairing service and cost data gives procurement a more complete basis for carrier negotiations.", "evidence_ids": ["seg:Carrier/Shipment ID:ratio:on_time_delivery", "seg:Carrier/Total Charge"]}]}, "analyst_view": {"methodology": "Cleaning (cleaning rules-v1): Parsed numbers or dates in 2 column(s). Merged label spelling variants in 1 column(s). Grouped missing labels as 'Unknown' in 1 column(s). Left missing values as missing in 2 column(s); nothing was imputed. Outliers flagged (kept) in: Fuel Surcharge, Linehaul, Total Charge, Weight. Final dataset: 3000 rows (started with 3000). Analysis (analysis v9) computed: eda, segment, source. Descriptive statistics use the non-missing values of each column.", "statistical_notes": ["Loaded 3,000 rows \u00d7 19 columns from a CSV file. (n = 3,000; high confidence: Read as-is: no layout guessing was needed.)", "on_time_delivery (from Shipment ID) by Carrier (5 groups) (n = 3,000; high confidence: 3000 rows)", "sum Total Charge by Carrier (5 groups) (n = 3,000; high confidence: 3000 rows)", "mean Total Charge by Carrier (5 groups) (n = 3,000; high confidence: 3000 rows)", "Weight: median 669.00, mean 1,129.37, range 1.54 to 8,754.20 (n = 2,995; high confidence: 2995 rows)", "Linehaul: median 147.62, mean 185.04, range 5.64 to 1,069.81 (n = 2,840; high confidence: 2840 rows)", "Fuel Surcharge: median 32.98, mean 41.72, range 1.30 to 258.09 (n = 2,840; high confidence: 2840 rows)", "Accessorials: median 0, mean 20.95, range 0 to 75.00 (n = 2,840; high confidence: 2840 rows)", "Total Charge: median 205.70, mean 247.72, range 6.94 to 1,338.03 (n = 2,840; high confidence: 2840 rows)"], "caveats": ["Each carrier's on-time rate reflects the mix of lanes, modes and shippers it handles in this dataset, not carrier capability in isolation; a direct performance comparison should control for those factors.", "102 rows in non-USD currencies and 62 cancelled rows are excluded from all figures, so carrier shipment counts and rates cover only the remaining USD shipments.", "The data spans 10 months (January through October 2026) with no prior-year equivalent, so it is not possible to tell whether current rates represent an improvement or decline.", "1 sentence(s) stating a cause or grading a result against a norm were removed: this data shows neither a controlled test nor an outside benchmark.", "Read as logistics data (on-time delivery, average transit time, cost per shipment, cost per lb, shipments). Rates pool their parts (on-time, OTIF, fill and cost per lb are totals divided, never averages of per-shipment rates). On time means on or before the promised date, dates as written (local); an early delivery is on time. Transit is in calendar days from the ship date. Cost is in the main currency only.", "62 cancelled rows are left out of every count and rate.", "The data covers 10 months, so month-over-month changes may be seasonal (a peak season); there is no same month last year to compare with.", "102 rows in currencies other than USD are left out of every figure, counts and on-time rates too, so the figures side by side read the same shipments.", "A carrier's figures depend on its lanes, modes and shippers: a difference between carriers is an association, not the carrier's doing, and every rate is given with its number of shipments.", "3 columns hold personal data; their values are masked before any model sees them.", "Weight: 837 weight values in kg (their Weight UOM) converted to lb: \u00d7 2.20462 + 0.", "Weight UOM: 837 rows' unit changed from kg to lb, with their values."], "code_references": ["df.groupby('Carrier')['Total Charge'].sum()", "df.groupby('Carrier')['Total Charge'].mean()"]}, "additional_issues_note": "", "generated_at": "2026-11-18 18:18:53.140527+00:00", "memory_used": []}}

