data: {"type": "expert_review", "data": {"review_summary": "10 claims checked against the evidence; none flagged.", "strengths": [], "gaps": ["The analysis does not break down on-time delivery by Shipping Mode, Destination City, or other lane characteristics, so it cannot identify which specific routes or modes are driving J.B. Hunt's and XPO's lower performance.", "No trend analysis across the 10-month period (January to October 2026) is shown, so seasonal patterns or month-over-month changes in carrier performance cannot be assessed.", "Shipment volume by carrier is not shown alongside on-time rates, making it unclear whether lower-performing carriers handle fewer, higher-complexity shipments that may explain their rates."], "next_investigations": ["Segment on-time delivery by Carrier and Shipping Mode to identify whether J.B. Hunt's and XPO's lower rates are concentrated in specific modes (e.g., LTL vs. TL).", "Compare on-time delivery by Carrier and Destination City to pinpoint geographic lanes where each carrier underperforms.", "Analyze on-time delivery by Carrier and Weight to determine whether heavier or lighter shipments correlate with late deliveries for lower-performing carriers."], "methodology_concerns": ["The on-time delivery rate excludes 102 rows in non-USD currencies and 62 cancelled rows, so the 88.9% overall rate and carrier comparisons apply only to USD shipments; the report does not state this limitation explicitly.", "Carrier differences in on-time rates are associations, not causal; the report correctly notes this in claim 2, but actions 7 and 8 frame carrier performance as the driver without accounting for the mix of lanes, modes, and shippers each carrier serves."], "flags": [], "generated_at": "2026-11-18T18:19:01.890119Z"}}

